            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Cementitious coatings like Thoroseal Waterproof Coating are specifically engineered for sustained hydrostatic pressure, such as groundwater pushing against a below-grade foundation or retaining wall. Penetrating silane-siloxane sealers like Foundation Armor SX5000 WB also perform well against moderate hydrostatic loads and add the benefit of remaining invisible, but for a wall actively fighting a high water table, a cementitious coating is the more appropriate rated solution.",
